# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Pack output
*.tgz

# Local experiments
*.local.*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# One checkout per change under review. A worktree is a second working tree for a
# branch that is still being written, so it is local tooling rather than anything
# this package carries.
.worktrees/

# Working notes that are not part of the project
#
# Competitive research, positioning drafts and the material under them are inputs
# to a decision, not documents the project maintains. They go stale within weeks
# and nothing published links to them, so they stay in the working tree and out of
# the repository. A published document may never link to one: `npm run check:parity`
# fails the build when it does.
positioning.md
competitive-analysis.md
research/
# The same goes for an audit's own report: it is an input to a fix, and what the
# repository keeps is the fix — the changelog entry and the code say what was wrong.
*-audit-report.md
*-query-report.md
# And for a proposal, which is an input to a decision record the way a report is an
# input to a fix. The record is written to stand on its own, so the draft that led to
# it is not kept: `internal/review-*.md` is the other case, and it is tracked because
# the review *is* the artifact rather than an input to one.
internal/proposal-*.md

# A comparison checkout of other plugins is the same kind of material — an input to a
# decision, and nothing published links to one. It is a whole source tree of somebody
# else's work, measured in hundreds of megabytes, and leaving it untracked-but-not-
# ignored means one `git add -A` commits it.
_compare/

# Worktrees are local scaffolding: one copy of this repository per branch, created and
# removed by `git worktree`. A branch never needs them, and they turn one `git add -A`
# into nine copies of the source tree.
.worktrees/

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
